# GitHub User Activity CLI
https://roadmap.sh/projects/github-user-activity

A simple command-line tool to fetch and display GitHub user activity using the GitHub API.

## About

This is an MVP (Minimum Viable Product) created to practice coding and learn software development concepts. It fetches recent activity for any GitHub user and displays it in a readable format.

## Prerequisites

You need a GitHub Personal Access Token to use this tool.

### Getting a GitHub Token:
1. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens
2. Click "Generate new token (classic)"
3. Give it a name and select scopes (public_repo is enough for public activity)
4. Copy the token

### Set up your token:
```bash
# Export your GitHub token as an environment variable
export GITHUB_TOKEN="your_token_here"

# Or add to your ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc to make it permanent
echo 'export GITHUB_TOKEN="your_token_here"' >> ~/.zshrc
source ~/.zshrc
```

## Installation

### Option 1: Direct Python Execution
Clone the repository and run directly:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/kristianfzr/github-user-activity.git
cd github-user-activity
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install requests
python3 -m github_user_activity.cli <username>
```

### Option 2: Install as CLI Tool
Install it globally so you can use `github-user-activity` command from anywhere:

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/kristianfzr/github-user-activity.git
cd github-user-activity

# Create and activate virtual environment
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

# Install in development mode
pip install -e .

# Now you can use it anywhere
github-user-activity <username>
```

## Usage

Once installed, simply provide a GitHub username:

```bash
# View activity for a user
github-user-activity kristianfzr
```

**Output example:**
```
- Pushed 3 commits to octocat/Hello-World
- Opened a new issue in octocat/Spoon-Knife
- Starred torvalds/linux
- Forked github/gitignore
- Created branch in octocat/test-repo
```

**Note:** If you haven't installed it as a CLI tool, run:
```bash
python3 -m github_user_activity.cli <username>
```

## Supported Event Types

- **PushEvent** - Code pushes
- **IssuesEvent** - Issue opened/closed
- **WatchEvent** - Repository starred
- **ForkEvent** - Repository forked
- **CreateEvent** - Branch/tag created
- **PullRequestEvent** - Pull request opened/closed
- **PullRequestReviewEvent** - PR reviewed
- **PullRequestReviewCommentEvent** - Commented on PR

## Troubleshooting

**"Error: GITHUB_TOKEN environment variable not set"**
- Make sure you've exported your token: `export GITHUB_TOKEN="your_token"`

**"Error fetching events: 401"**
- Your token might be invalid or expired. Generate a new one.

**"Error fetching events: 404"**
- The username doesn't exist or the user has no public activity.
